<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38596" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπέλ-ευσις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>coming on</i> or <i>to, arrival,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄχλων</span>”
				<i>Cat.Cod. Astr.</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					7.132
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1574.59
			</span></i>; <i>touching on</i> a thing, <i>survey</i> of it, Id. ad <i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i> P. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Prooem.</u>
				p.71
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i>; so [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέγεθος] ἐν διεξόδῳ καὶ ἐ. καθ᾽
					ἕκαστον μέρος αἰσθανόμεθα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plot.
					2.8.1
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Them.
			</span></i><i>in de An.</i><i><span class="en">
				30.33
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>adventitious impulse,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Chrysipp.Stoic.
				2.282
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> in Law,
				<i>prosecution,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PFay.
				26.14
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				1638.13
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A. D.)</span>.</div>
